:: Faking It [event sister_quest] {"position":"3150,1400","size":"100,100"}
The college hallway is almost empty at this hour, just the fluorescent tubes buzzing overhead and a janitor's cart parked outside the restrooms. I type the professor's name into my phone as I walk. There's a faculty page, a couple of dusty articles, and one line I read twice: $prof.callName sits on the curriculum committee and has a say in scholarships and transfers. So he's a bitter math teacher who enjoys handing out C's and also gets a vote on where the scholarship money goes, which makes him a lot more interesting to me than he was a minute ago.

His office door has a laminated sign that says OFFICE HOURS TUE 2-3, and it is very much not Tuesday. I push it open without knocking. The room is small and smells like old paper and instant coffee. There are books on the shelves, on the floor and on top of the filing cabinet, stacked wherever gravity allowed it. A desk lamp throws a yellow circle onto the desk, and in the middle of it sits $prof.callName behind his laptop, balding head shining, wire-rimmed glasses halfway down his nose. He looks up at me the way people look at a fly that got into the car.

<<Image "images/characters/sister/events/faking it/prof_sitting.jpg" "" "" 500>>

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
{ who: $prof, text: "May I help you? Office hours, as the sign on the door makes abundantly clear, are on Tuesdays. If you have a question about the course, you may email me like everyone else." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm not here about class. I'm here about $sister.name $sister.surname, one of your calculus students." },
{ who: $prof, text: "Miss $sister.surname. And what about her? If you are yet another friend come to plead for extra credit, spare us both the embarrassment. She will earn her grade like everyone else, or she will not." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
I close the door behind me. There's a chair for visitors, with a stack of ungraded papers on it, so I stay standing.
<<linkreplace "Turn on $company.prototype.name">>
I slide the prototype out of my pocket and switch it on while he's still glaring at me. <<UseQuestDevice $sister>> It settles into its quiet hum, and I keep my voice slow and even, the way you'd talk to a dog you haven't made up your mind about.
<<Video "images/characters/player/prototype/pocket_pull_out.mp4" "" "" 500>>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs to [
{ who: $player, text: "She's been really stressed lately, and you've been pretty hard on her. I'd like you to make sure she passes the next test." },
{ who: $prof, text: "Make sure she passes? Absolutely not. I do not hand out grades, young man. If she cannot handle the material, that is her problem and not mine." },
{ text: "He leans back and folds his arms. There's a particular kind of sourness in his face, the kind a man collects over decades of being a little less important than he thinks he should be." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm not asking you to hand her anything. I'm offering a trade. I can get her to dress a lot more... memorably in your class. Shorter skirts, lower tops, the kind of outfits I'm guessing you already notice. Every single day." },
{ who: $prof, text: "Excuse me?" },
{ text: "His eyes narrow, but they don't leave mine, and he doesn't tell me to get out. The hum keeps working on him, smoothing the edges off his outrage before it can turn into anything useful." },
{ who: $player, text: "And if you help her pass, there'll be more for you later. More than you'd believe if I told you now." },
{ who: $prof, text: "You are serious. You are actually standing in my office, uninvited, and making me that offer." },
{ text: "He stares at me for a long moment. Then he lets out a short, tired laugh, like a man who has been waiting years for the world to finally prove him right." },
{ who: $prof, text: "I have taught at this institution for eighteen years, Mr...? No, don't tell me, I would rather not know. Eighteen years of students who could not care less about the subject, and the young women are the worst of them, convinced that a smile and a short skirt ought to open every door. And now here you are, offering me precisely that. Very well. She passes the next examination. I shall, however, expect a noticeable improvement in the wardrobe, and should this 'more' of yours ever materialize, I will remember who promised it." },
{ who: $player, text: "You'll get what you want. Just make sure her grade holds up." },
{ who: $prof, text: "Then we understand each other. Now kindly get out of my office." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>
I give him a small nod and let myself out. Out in the hallway the janitor's cart is gone. I switch the prototype off, drop it back into my pocket and take my time on the way to the exit, past a bulletin board full of tutoring flyers that nobody is going to call.
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 6>>
